Let $A\subseteq \mathbb{R}$, let $f:A\to\mathbb{R}$, and let $c\in A$. The following are equivalent:
\begin{enumerate}
\item $c$ is a point of discontinuity in the $\varepsilon$-$\delta$ sense.
\item $c$ is a sequential point of discontinuity.
