Let \(E\) be a subset of a metric space \(X\).  Then \(E^\circ\) is the
largest open subset of \(X\) contained in \(E\).  In other words:
\begin{enumerate}
  \item \(E^\circ\subseteq E\);
  \item \(E^\circ\) is open;
  \item \(E^\circ\supseteq O\), for every open set \(O\subseteq E\).
\end{enumerate}

