Then $U$ is a subspace of $V$ if and only if the following three conditions hold:
\begin{enumerate}[label=(\roman*)]
  \item $0 \in U$;
  \item for all $u,v \in U$, one has $u+v \in U$;
  \item for all $a \in \mathbf{F}$ and all $u \in U$, one has $au \in U$.
\end{enumerate}

